    "reversed": "Reversed, the work may lose its meaning or its balance. It can show repetitive effort without growth, cutting corners, or boredom with a skill you once loved. It can also point to perfectionism, polishing the same piece forever, or to working so much that the rest of life is neglected. Sometimes it means you are not yet ready to master something and need more of the basics first. Ask whether your effort is serving your growth or just filling time."
